GV) Alcoholic Beverage consumption regulated; Drinking in Public

- (a) It shall be unlawful for any person to drink any. intoxicating beverage in any street or sidewalk within the city.

- (b) It shall be unlawful to possess any intoxicating beverage within any public park or on the premises of any publicly owned recreation center within the city.

(c} It shall be unlawful for any person to drink any intoxicating beverages on the outside of any commercial establishment on the property thereof.

- (d) It shall be unlawful for any person to possess an open container of any intoxicating beverage while operating a vehicle on the public streets, rights-of-way or other public property in the city or while a passenger in or on a vehicle being operated in the public streets, rights-of-way or other public properties in the city.

- qd) As used herein, the term "open container" means any container, the contents of which are immediately capable of being consumed or any container the seal of which has been broken.

- (2) An open container shall be considered to be in the possession of ihe operator of a vehicle if the container is not in the possession of a passenger and is not located in a locked glove compartment, locked trunk or otherwise inaccessible. A container is inaccessible within the meaning of this subsection if it is accessible to neither the driver or any other person in the vehicle, which such driver and other persons are seated in the vehicle.

- (3) An open container shall be considered to be in the possession of a passenger of a vehicle if the container is in the physical control of the passenger. (4) This subsection shall not apply to the following: (a) A passenger of a vehicle in which the driver is operating the vehicle pursuant to a contract to provide transportation for passengers and such driver holds a valid chauffeur's license pursuant to state jaw or that of any other state. (b) A passenger of a bus in which the driver holds a valid chauffeur's license pursuant to state law or that of any other state.

